---
description: >-
  Reverie atmosphere engine: per-character worlds driven by conversation parameters. Read before
  changing src/theme/** or any screen that shows a character.
alwaysApply: false
globs: ["src/theme/**", "src/screens/**", "src/components/**"]
---

# Atmosphere rules

- Every screen that shows a character calls `setTheme(theme, scene)` and sets the conversation
  parameters (`setParam('typing'|'drag'|'affinity')`), the pulses (`pulse('gust'|'bloom')`) and the
  next-world preview (`setPreview`) through `useFrameTheme()`. A screen owns WHEN; `src/theme/` owns
  what each world does in response.
- Never write CSS custom properties per frame. Per-frame parameter changes go into refs the
  atmosphere loop reads; a registered custom property write forces a style recalc of the whole
  subtree (web.dev measured ~3.9ms on a 1000-element tree). The `--t-*` colors tween only on a theme
  change.
- `backdrop-filter` belongs to the floating controls only (tab bar, chat menu button, deck buttons,
  at most 12px). Bubbles, rows, cards and sheets use an opaque or >= 0.86 alpha surface: a blurred
  layer over the live canvas is re-blurred every frame.
- The app deliberately ignores `prefers-reduced-motion` (the user's instruction: "do not respect
  reduced motion"). Every animation, particle field, portrait loop and clip always plays; motion's
  `MotionConfig reducedMotion="never"` and the `useReducedMotion` helper in `src/lib/motion.ts`
  (always false) enforce it. Do not add reduced-motion fallbacks back.
- Theme palettes live in `src/theme/themes.ts`; atmosphere tints too (hex values are allowed there
  and nowhere else in components). Each world keeps its contrast checks passing over its own plate.
- The atmosphere is modelled on game-audio RTPC: conversation params (`typing`, `drag`, `affinity`),
  pulses (`gust`, `bloom`) and `setPreview` drive per-world response curves. That lateral was chosen
  because incumbents have no conversation-driven world (Telegram moves one fixed wallpaper per send;
  character apps offer static or looped backgrounds). Keep the curves; do not replace the mechanism
  with per-screen special cases.
- No per-frame CSS custom property writes: params go through refs into the atmosphere loop. Reason:
  registered properties recalc the subtree on every write (web.dev @property benchmark).
